{"status":"ready","content":"To compute $987654321^2$ exactly, we multiply $987654321 \\times 987654321$.\nWe can write $987654321 = 10^9 - 12345679$.\nWe can also rewrite it as $(10^9 - 12345679)$.\nThen we have\n$$987654321^2 = (10^9 - 12345679)(10^9 - 12345679)$$\n$$= (10^9)^2 - 2(10^9)(12345679) + (12345679)^2$$\n$$= 10^{18} - 24691358 \\times 10^9 + (12345679)^2$$\nNow, we can compute $(12345679)^2$ without using a calculator.\n\nAlternatively, we can write $987654321 = 10^9 - 12345679$.\nThen $987654321 = \\frac{8888888888}{9}$.\nThen $987654321^2 = (\\frac{8888888888}{9})^2 = \\frac{790123456790123456}{81}$\n$987654321^2 = (\\frac{8888888888}{9})^2$\n$987654321^2 = (\\frac{8888888888}{9}) \\times (\\frac{8888888888}{9})$\nThis method is messy.\nLet $x = 987654321$.\nThen $x^2 = (987654321)^2 = 975463078456$.\nConsider the pattern:\n$1^2 = 1$\n$11^2 = 121$\n$111^2 = 12321$\n$1111^2 = 1234321$\n$11111^2 = 123454321$\n$111111^2 = 12345654321$\n$1111111^2 = 1234567654321$\n$11111111^2 = 123456787654321$\n$111111111^2 = 12345679012345679012345678^2= 12345678987654321$\n$9^2 = 81$\n$99^2 = 9801$\n$999^2 = 998001$\n$9999^2 = 99980001$\n$987654321^2 = 975308641975308641$.\n\nWe can write $x = 10^9 - 12345679$.\nThen $x^2 = (10^9 - 12345679)^2 = 10^{18} - 2(12345679)(10^9) + (12345679)^2$\n$10^{18} - 2469135800000000000 + 15241578750190521$\nIf we do this by hand, we get $975308641^2$.\n$987654321^2 = 975308642006321$\n$= 975308641975308641$.\n\n$987654321^2 = 975308642006321$.\n$987654321^2 = 975308641975308641$\n$975308641975308641$\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $\\boxed{975308641975308641}$\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Gemini 2.0 Flash Lite","modelId":"google/gemini-2.0-flash-lite-001","promptId":"31-own-Large-Square","content":"To compute $987654321^2$ exactly, we multiply $987654321 \\times 987654321$.\nWe can write $987654321 = 10^9 - 12345679$.\nWe can also rewrite it as $(10^9 - 12345679)$.\nThen we have\n$$987654321^2 = (10^9 - 12345679)(10^9 - 12345679)$$\n$$= (10^9)^2 - 2(10^9)(12345679) + (12345679)^2$$\n$$= 10^{18} - 24691358 \\times 10^9 + (12345679)^2$$\nNow, we can compute $(12345679)^2$ without using a calculator.\n\nAlternatively, we can write $987654321 = 10^9 - 12345679$.\nThen $987654321 = \\frac{8888888888}{9}$.\nThen $987654321^2 = (\\frac{8888888888}{9})^2 = \\frac{790123456790123456}{81}$\n$987654321^2 = (\\frac{8888888888}{9})^2$\n$987654321^2 = (\\frac{8888888888}{9}) \\times (\\frac{8888888888}{9})$\nThis method is messy.\nLet $x = 987654321$.\nThen $x^2 = (987654321)^2 = 975463078456$.\nConsider the pattern:\n$1^2 = 1$\n$11^2 = 121$\n$111^2 = 12321$\n$1111^2 = 1234321$\n$11111^2 = 123454321$\n$111111^2 = 12345654321$\n$1111111^2 = 1234567654321$\n$11111111^2 = 123456787654321$\n$111111111^2 = 12345679012345679012345678^2= 12345678987654321$\n$9^2 = 81$\n$99^2 = 9801$\n$999^2 = 998001$\n$9999^2 = 99980001$\n$987654321^2 = 975308641975308641$.\n\nWe can write $x = 10^9 - 12345679$.\nThen $x^2 = (10^9 - 12345679)^2 = 10^{18} - 2(12345679)(10^9) + (12345679)^2$\n$10^{18} - 2469135800000000000 + 15241578750190521$\nIf we do this by hand, we get $975308641^2$.\n$987654321^2 = 975308642006321$\n$= 975308641975308641$.\n\n$987654321^2 = 975308642006321$.\n$987654321^2 = 975308641975308641$\n$975308641975308641$\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $\\boxed{975308641975308641}$\n","inferredMetadata":{"inferred":true,"sourcePath":"scripts/responses/gemini-2-0-flash-lite/31-own-Large-Square.json","modelSlug":"gemini-2-0-flash-lite","modelFamily":"google_commodity","modelReleaseDate":"Feb 2025","modelSource":"openrouter"},"prompt":{"id":"31-own-Large-Square","text":"Compute 987654321 squared exactly.","tags":["reasoning","math"]}},"path":"responses/gemini-2-0-flash-lite/31-own-Large-Square.json","size":2207,"mtime":1779394310}